--- source/en/manuals/distributions/nixos.txt
+++ candidate/en/manuals/distributions/nixos.txt
@@ -29,6 +29,41 @@
 It is possible to deploy custom configuration using vpsAdmin on VPS creation and reinstallation,
 see [[manuals:vps:userdata|user data]].
 
+===== Container configuration =====
+For stable NixOS releases, include the compatibility module in your flake's
+''modules'' list:
+
+<code nix>
+vpsadminos.nixosModules.containerStable
+</code>
+
+It selects the module using your ''nixpkgs'' release. When upgrading to another
+registered stable release, keep this import and update the ''nixpkgs'' input.
+Keep the ''vpsadminos'' input up to date too. If its pinned revision does not
+include your release, evaluation fails and lists the available releases.
+''system.stateVersion'' controls compatibility with existing state; it does not
+select this module and normally stays unchanged during a NixOS upgrade.
+
+You can also select a release explicitly or look it up using the release string:
+
+<code nix>
+vpsadminos.nixosModules.containers."26.05"
+vpsadminos.nixosModules.containers.${nixpkgs.lib.trivial.release}
+</code>
+
+Each line is an alternative module import. ''containers'' is a lookup map;
+import a release entry. The older names such as ''container_26_05'' remain
+available. ''nixosModules.container'' is an alias of ''containerStable''.
+For NixOS unstable, explicitly use ''vpsadminos.nixosModules.containerUnstable''.
+The stable selector does not detect the unstable channel.
+
+Existing VPS configurations are not rewritten automatically. If your flake uses
+an older release-specific import, update the vpsAdminOS input and switch the
+import to ''containerStable'' while keeping your nixpkgs pin and stateVersion.
+You can then upgrade nixpkgs separately. For the module reference and the
+standalone-file configuration, see
+[[https://vpsadminos.org/containers/nixos/|NixOS guest configuration]].
+
 ===== VPS management =====
 See the [[:home|VPS manuals]] for more information about our infrastructure and possibilities.
 
